---
// Clef's lanes: one reading per change decides how much of the workflow it gets.
---

<div class="pl-wrap">
  <div class="pl-routing">
    <div class="fx-node fx-in" data-c="grey" style="--d:0">
      A change<small>from your prompt</small>
    </div>
    <span class="fx-arrow fx-in" style="--d:300" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <div class="fx-node fx-in" data-c="amber" style="--d:450">
      Clef<small>reads it once</small>
    </div>
    <span class="fx-arrow fx-in" style="--d:750" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <div class="pl-branches">
      <div class="pl-branch fx-in" data-c="green" style="--d:900">
        <span class="pl-out" data-c="green">
          the checks can prove it, in one place
        </span>
        <div class="fx-node" data-c="teal">
          Fast path<small>one worker · your checks prove it</small>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="pl-branch fx-in" data-c="grey" style="--d:1150">
        <span class="pl-out" data-c="grey">
          any doubt
        </span>
        <div class="fx-node" data-c="teal">
          Full workflow<small>plan · worker · gate · judge</small>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="pl-branch fx-in" data-c="amber" style="--d:1400">
        <span class="pl-out" data-c="amber">
          a mistake could pass the tests
        </span>
        <div class="fx-node" data-c="teal">
          Second reviewer<small>the workflow + another model</small>
        </div>
        <span class="pl-when">
          If a fast-path change breaks a check or turns out risky, it moves to
          the full workflow and carries on from there.
        </span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="pl-routing-foot fx-in" style="--d:1700">
    <span class="fx-chip" data-c="grey" data-wrap>
      every seat runs at the model and level you choose
    </span>
    <span class="fx-chip" data-c="grey" data-wrap>
      the judge never shares a model with the writer
    </span>
  </div>
</div>
